# Tooling: Claude Code Plugin Third-Party Skill Porting

## Overview

| Field | Value |
| ------- | ------- |
| **Date** | 2026-03-28 |
| **Objective** | Integrate obra/superpowers methodology skills into ProjectHephaestus without license violations |
| **Outcome** | Successful — 8 additive skills ported, 4 redundant skills skipped, MIT attribution applied, PR #206 opened |
| **Verification** | verified-precommit — PR open, CI not yet confirmed |
| **Source** | HomericIntelligence/ProjectHephaestus#206, https://github.com/obra/superpowers |

## When to Use

- Evaluating whether to adopt skills from an open-source Claude Code plugin
- Deciding between: install as separate plugin, fork/vendor, or port select skills
- Porting skills with hardcoded paths or unknown tooling into your project's conventions
- Applying MIT license attribution
- Designing a meta-skill (skill-advisor) as an alternative to SessionStart hooks

## Verified Workflow

### Quick Reference

```bash
gh repo clone <org>/<repo> /tmp/source-repo
ls /tmp/source-repo/
ls <your-plugin>/skills/
python3 scripts/validate_plugins.py
```

### Integration Approach Decision Tree

| Approach | When to Use | Risk |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Install as separate plugin | No overlap AND no hook conflicts | SessionStart hook conflicts |
| Fork/vendor | Need all skills AND can maintain a fork | High — ongoing sync burden |
| Port select skills | Only need subset AND source has hardcoded conventions | Low |

### Overlap Analysis

| Superpowers Skill | Decision | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| subagent-driven-development | SKIP | myrmidon-swarm is superior |
| dispatching-parallel-agents | SKIP | Covered by myrmidon-swarm |
| writing-skills | SKIP | Covered by learn + Mnemosyne |
| test-driven-development | PORT | Additive |
| systematic-debugging | PORT | Additive |
| verification-before-completion | PORT | Additive |
| using-git-worktrees | PORT | Additive |
| finishing-a-development-branch | PORT | Additive |
| brainstorming | PORT | Additive |
| requesting-code-review + receiving-code-review + agents/code-reviewer.md | PORT (merged) | Additive — combined into single skill |
| using-superpowers (meta) | ADAPT | Becomes skill-advisor meta-skill |

### Adaptation Checklist

```
[ ] Add Mnemosyne integration: auto-invoke /advise at task start, suggest /learn at end
[ ] Add cross-references to myrmidon-swarm phases
[ ] Align git commands: conventional commits, gh pr create, protected-main
[ ] Add project tooling refs: pixi run pytest, pixi run mypy, pixi run ruff
[ ] Change hardcoded spec paths
[ ] Change worktree defaults to /tmp/<project>-<branch>
[ ] Add MIT attribution footer
[ ] Convert to Hephaestus YAML frontmatter format
[ ] Validate with scripts/validate_plugins.py
```

### MIT License Attribution

Add this footer to every ported skill file:
  *Adapted from obra/superpowers under MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025 Jesse Vincent.*

## Failed Attempts

| Attempt | What Was Tried | Why It Failed | Lesson Learned |
| --------- | ---------------- | --------------- | ---------------- |
| Install superpowers as separate plugin | Would add all 14 skills without modification | SessionStart hook conflicts with ai-maestro hooks | Check for hook conflicts before choosing separate plugin installation |
| Fork/vendor superpowers | Maintain full upstream compatibility | Forking a 120K-star rapidly-evolving repo creates sync burden for only 7 needed skills | Prefer selective porting over forking for subsets |
| Direct copy without adaptation | Save time on each skill port | superpowers hardcodes docs/superpowers/specs/ paths, doesn't reference Mnemosyne or pixi tooling | Always audit for hardcoded paths and project-specific tooling |
| Merging code-review into two separate skills | Matched superpowers' split | Redundant — reviewer persona and both sides belong together | Consolidate closely-related source skills into one ported skill |

